G6a-9 changes remain uncommitted. No push or service deployment.

User scope:
  Continue implementation first; postpone long-running verification.
  This turn ran local unit/race/project validation only.
  No 4-hour/24-hour soak test, remote run, new automation, container start,
  Gateway/Server/Proxy/Agent deployment or production traffic change.

Implemented:
  Per-run control; graceful shutdown separately cancels the capture root,
  joins it and freezes the final durable local tail before draining cold.
  Drain success requires exact lineage/position and GC confirmation, with
  explicit empty-log and snapshot-only exceptions.
  Deadline forces only its generation; manual caller cancellation has its own
  shutdown_aborted category; pending/terminal errors are never replaced.
  Done closes only after capture/ACK and both run ownership locks are released.
  Read-only Prometheus collector: one snapshot per scrape, explicit registry,
  fixed labels, validity for positions/lag/timestamps/disk availability.
  No service HTTP/config registration or data-plane activation.

Review fixes:
  Publish stop request before canceling source; otherwise captureDone could
  race ahead and be misclassified as ordinary cancellation.
  Preserve errors.Join(terminal, context.Canceled): neither force-timeout nor
  normal-stop classification may hide an uncertain/corrupt/full outcome.
  Terminal markers also take precedence over source/cold retry markers.
  Clear prior run/control observations on a failed new start.
  Sampling failure reports AvailableKnown=false, distinct from actual zero.

Pre-final test issue:
  Initial whole-gateway race run failed in
    TestSyncRunnerShutdownJoinedTerminalAndCancellationRemainFatal/final_drain_corrupt
    sync_runner_shutdown_test.go:621: shutdown test did not reach controlled boundary
  The fault test used a 35ms deadline that could expire while the final captured
  frame was fsyncing, before reaching its intended cold-I/O boundary.
  Corrected the test to wait on an explicit boundary and then force that exact
  run with shutdown_timeout; separate actual deadline tests remain in place.
  This fixes fault-injection timing; no terminal result assertion was relaxed.

